<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xu Shuzheng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1880–1925</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xu Shuzheng was a Chinese general and politician of the Anhui clique during the Beiyang period. In 1919 he led troops into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulaanbaatar">Urga</a> and forced the abolition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/outer-mongolia">Outer Mongolia</a>'s autonomy, but his rule there collapsed when the Anhui clique lost power in 1920. He was assassinated in 1925.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xu-shuzheng.jpg" alt="Xu Shuzheng" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges Chevalier · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1925_Xu_Shuzheng.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
